# showtime core Python dependencies (Python 3.12, installed by setup.py into ~/.showtime/venv).
#
# Edit THIS file, then regenerate the universal lock (one file, all platforms):
#   uv pip compile --universal --python-version 3.12 \
#       --index-url https://pypi.org/simple requirements.in -o requirements.txt
#
# Not in the default install (fetched on first use, see manifest.json "lazy_pip"):
#   requirements-whisper.in          faster-whisper + ctranslate2, before the first Whisper transcription
#   requirements-imageio-ffmpeg.txt  imageio-ffmpeg, only when neither the static nor a system ffmpeg works
#
# Platform notes (PEP 508 markers):
# - Intel Macs (darwin/x86_64) are frozen at the last releases that ship x86_64
#   wheels: onnxruntime 1.23.2, numba 0.62.1, llvmlite 0.45.1 (numba 0.62 caps numpy < 2.4).
#   Every other platform gets the current releases.
# - tinysoundfont is installed separately with --no-deps (its metadata pulls pyaudio,
#   which is only needed for live playback); it has no wheel for Intel macOS or
#   Linux arm64, where it builds from source (needs a C compiler) or is skipped.

